Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:30:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1129/1265] A renamed probe still found by the sheet (1166,
 part nine)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor: «смело переименовывай все треки в законченных 💎 воркспейсах. Под единый стиль». The
instruments' sheet found an instrument's probes, ▶ A and ▶ B, its picture and its verdict by the
take's title (probe60-SLUG-a/b); a probe renamed for the public (Harp · A) would have left every
instrument «not identified». It falls back on the take's own name, which a rename never changes
(the title first, so the probes renamed into Styles on purpose, probe60-orchestral-a/b, stay
where they are).

cdp-console 316/0/7, check-i18n 14/0, check-player 3/0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/console/heresy-instruments.js | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/console/heresy-instruments.js b/tools/console/heresy-instruments.js
index 4fb30f4..8560824 100644
--- a/tools/console/heresy-instruments.js
+++ b/tools/console/heresy-instruments.js
@@ -28,7 +28,8 @@
   function probes(slug) {
     var out = {}, rank = {};
     state.rows.forEach(function (r) {
-      var m = /^(probe|style)(60|120)-(.+)-([ab])$/.exec(r.title || "");
+      // HERESY 1166: a probe renamed for the public (Harp · A) is found by the take's own name, which a rename never changes
+      var re = /^(probe|style)(60|120)-(.+)-([ab])$/, m = re.exec(r.title || "") || re.exec(String(r.name || "").replace(/^\d{8}-\d{6}-/, ""));
       if (!m || m[3] !== slug) return;
       var k = (m[1] === "style" ? 1000 : 0) + +m[2];
       if (!out[m[4]] || k > rank[m[4]]) { out[m[4]] = r; rank[m[4]] = k; }
